    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for cpp-httplib",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for cpp-httplib fixes the following issues\n\n- CVE-2026-21428: server-side request forgery via header injection (bsc#1255835).\n- CVE-2026-22776: unsafe handling of compressed HTTP request can cause a denial of service (bsc#1256518).\n- CVE-2026-28434: default exception handler may leak e.what() to clients via EXCEPTION_WHAT response header\n  (bsc#1259221).\n- CVE-2026-28435: payload size limit bypass via gzip decompression in ContentReader (streaming) can lead to denial of\n  service (bsc#1259220).\n- CVE-2026-29076: denial of service via crafted HTTP POST request (bsc#1259373).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "openSUSE-Leap-16.0-724",
